```java
public static class ProcessReturnInfo {
    public int exitCode;
    public String stdout;
    public String stderr;
}

public static ProcessReturnInfo executeCommand(String command) throws IOException {
    Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);
    ByteArrayOutputStream stdoutStream = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
    ByteArrayOutputStream stderrStream = new ByteArrayOutputStream();

    try (InputStream stdoutIn = process.getInputStream();
         InputStream stderrIn = process.getErrorStream()) {

        stdoutIn.transferTo(stdoutStream);
        stderrIn.transferTo(stderrStream);

        int exitCode = process.waitFor();

        ProcessReturnInfo result = new ProcessReturnInfo();
        result.exitCode = exitCode;
        result.stdout = stdoutStream.toString("UTF-8");
        result.stderr = stderrStream.toString("UTF-8");

        return result;
    }
}
```

This method creates a `Process` object using the given command, and then captures the output and error streams. It then waits for the process to complete using the `waitFor()` method, which returns the exit code of the process. The captured output and error streams are converted to strings and stored in the `ProcessReturnInfo` object, which is then returned.

```java
public static String generateJson(Object obj) {
    StringBuilder json = new StringBuilder();
    if (obj == null) {
        json.append("null");
    } else if (obj instanceof String) {
        json.append(quote((String) obj));
    } else if (obj instanceof Number) {
        json.append(obj.toString());
    } else if (obj instanceof Boolean) {
        json.append(((Boolean) obj) ? "true" : "false");
    } else if (obj instanceof Object[]) {
        json.append("[");
        for (Object o : (Object[]) obj) {
            json.append(generateJson(o));
            json.append(",");
        }
        int len = ((Object[]) obj).length;
        if (len > 0) {
            json.setCharAt(json.length() - 1, ']');
        } else {
            json.append("]");
        }
    } else if (obj instanceof Map) {
        json.append("{");
        boolean first = true;
        for (Map.Entry<String, Object> entry : (Map<String, Object>) obj.entrySet()) {
            if (!first) {
                json.append(",");
            } else {
                first = false;
            }
            json.append(quote(entry.getKey()));
            json.append(":");
            json.append(generateJson(entry.getValue()));
        }
        json.append("}");
    } else {
        throw new JSONException("Unsupported type: " + obj.getClass());
    }
    return json.toString();

}

private static String quote(String s) {
    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
        char c = s.charAt(i);
        if (c == '"' || c == '\\') {
            sb.append("\\");
        }
        sb.append(c);
    }
    return "\"" + sb.toString() + "\"";
}

class JSONException extends Exception {
    public JSONException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
